1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,800
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:22,080
He was unquestionably the greatest Meister to ever graduate from the Academy, Dr. Frankenstein.

3
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,660
He's a tough one.

4
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:30,300
So this Meister was your weapon Death Scythe's first partner.

5
00:00:30,620 --> 00:00:33,300
And wait, you sent a group of students to go collect his soul?

6
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,660
He should send you, big sis. You could do it.

7
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,200
Only if I really felt like dying.

8
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,660
You're overestimating me a little bit, Patty.

9
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:43,660
I wouldn't last two seconds.

10
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:46,580
These are remedial lessons, right?

11
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,960
Aren't you asking a bit too much?

12
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,440
You know what's going to happen.

13
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:55,000
They'll die.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:12,560
I'll see you later.

15
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:19,660
A firmware sound that one will make him proper.

16
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:25,760
Can I hear enough?

17
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:42,700
Six人目も合わさず運命まで絡んでく

18
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:47,920
行き先もらったポテル食えない夜の端で

19
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:53,780
不可愛しすぎた眩しさが

20
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:57,780
悪い夢に続いても

21
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:05,120
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら

22
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:11,900
言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

23
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:17,020
出会った理由は途絶びに突きつけられて

24
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:22,980
触れた瞬間の傷の分だけ確かになれる

25
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:32,100
So this is where we find Stein

26
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:34,740
Let's hurry and finish this guy off

27
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,520
I'm ready for these lessons to be over

28
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:44,560
He even put zigzag stitches on his laboratory

29
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:53,880
Interesting architecture

30
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,040
I wonder what kind of guy this Stein is

31
00:02:56,040 --> 00:03:07,380
Something's coming out of there

32
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:21,420
Damn it

33
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:23,380
Still doesn't feel quite right

34
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:28,000
Maybe that'll take care of it

35
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,540
Okay I'm gonna try that again

36
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:35,580
Um shouldn't someone stop him

37
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:37,620
But we just met him isn't that rude

38
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:39,500
I'd like to see what happens next

39
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,620
Yeah so would I

40
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:50,380
Is this guy for real?

41
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,660
It's not

42
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:56,620
Shape of the soul

43
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:58,940
Enter the ultimate meister Stein

44
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:07,660
Was there something you kids needed me for?

45
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:10,560
Yeah if you're really Dr. Stein

46
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,460
You did this

47
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:13,520
You're the one who turned Sid into a zombie

48
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,560
Oh

49
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,560
So that's it

50
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:19,860
I'm guessing you guys are all students from the academy then

51
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,460
Why did you do this?

52
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:22,200
Revenge?

53
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:22,980
A grudge?

54
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,360
No nothing like that

55
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,140
I have a simpler motive

56
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,760
Experimentation and observation

57
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:29,960
That's all a true scientist cares about

58
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:32,060
And I am a scientist

59
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:35,620
Everything in the world is an experimental test subject

60
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:37,860
Of course that includes myself as well

61
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:44,320
Hey do you feel that soul?

62
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,160
I think something strange is happening

63
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,080
Huh?

64
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:47,960
Like what?

65
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,300
Your soul's wavelengths aren't very stable

66
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,580
What's more they're quite different from one another

67
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:56,520
I see one soul that is careless and arrogant

68
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,760
And one that is earnest and strong-willed

69
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:02,580
They appear to be in resonance but they aren't

70
00:05:02,580 --> 00:05:03,400
What the hell?

71
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:06,240
You mean you can see the soul of someone who's still alive?

72
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:08,240
In that case you must be a meister

73
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,680
He was able to read the character of the souls too

74
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,560
Only the best meisters can do that

75
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,880
So what?

76
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,700
Maka you can see souls clearly like that too right?

77
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,220
Oh, of course I can

78
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:23,580
Your soul seems confused by that last statement

79
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:24,580
How cute

80
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:25,240
Shut up!

81
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:25,740
Quit it!

82
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:27,080
Stop looking at my soul you creep!

83
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,760
Yeah shut up little doctor man

84
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,760
No one wants to hear you talk anymore

85
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:31,520
Yahoo!

86
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:35,380
How about we change the subject to a more interesting conversation topic

87
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:36,720
Like me for example

88
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,020
When did he

89
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,180
Who cares if you can see souls?

90
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,360
What does that matter, huh?

91
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:43,600
Not like you're gonna see anything interesting

92
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,900
Far as I'm concerned

93
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,820
The only soul worth looking at is mine

94
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:51,080
Yours is an interesting one

95
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,820
Your soul is extremely self-centered

96
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,200
And more than a little bit wild

97
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:58,420
It must be rather difficult to find a partner

98
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:00,280
With a soul that's compatible with your own

99
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:00,780
Isn't it?

100
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,040
No more talking

101
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:11,060
Black star!

102
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:12,100
Hmm?

103
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,800
Ah yes, I see it now

104
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:17,100
You must be the wild ones, partner

105
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:19,300
You're always willing to compromise

106
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,180
And possess a very accepting nature

107
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:23,060
It makes sense that you're the one

108
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,420
Who's able to cooperate with his soul's wavelength

109
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:28,220
Who do you think you are, old man?

110
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:31,840
Now that I've collected the necessary initial data from all of you

111
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:34,240
I think we're ready to begin the experiment

112
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:38,660
Looks like we've run out of sake!

113
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:41,340
You drink so fast I can hardly keep up

114
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:43,120
Hold on, just a sec

115
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,260
Pump, pump, pumpkin, pumpkin

116
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,140
And up we go!

117
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,160
Blair, you're already so good at this

118
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,040
And it's only your third day working here

119
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,220
I would have guessed you've been here forever

120
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:53,680
Really?

121
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,140
Aw, thank you!

122
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:57,380
You went to the school today, didn't you?

123
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:58,340
How'd it go?

124
00:06:58,640 --> 00:06:59,640
How are things with Maka?

125
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:04,540
Me!

126
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,280
She ignored me

127
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:08,040
Oh, poor thing

128
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,700
It doesn't matter what I do

129
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,200
She just gets angry

130
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:13,080
Maka is such a darling girl

131
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:16,460
Anyway, your divorce from her mother was finalized last month, wasn't it?

132
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,520
It's time to move on

133
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,240
Let's see if we can cheer you up, okay?

134
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:21,720
What do I have to be cheerful about?

135
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:23,820
Custody goes to the mother

136
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:25,100
My wife

137
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:28,380
No, no, my ex-wife won't let me contribute anything

138
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,240
No alimony or medical expenses

139
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:33,120
What can I ever be to Maka now?

140
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:36,120
I'm a father without any fatherly duties

141
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,580
Doesn't mean you're not her dad

142
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:40,180
Being a parent is about more than just money, isn't it?

143
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:41,420
You should fight for her

144
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,600
But spending money is a way of expressing love too, right?

145
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,880
It's so frustrating not being able to do anything for her

146
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,560
Okay, then think about it this way

147
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,660
With all that extra money

148
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:53,220
You'll be able to indulge in your bad habits more than usual

149
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:55,220
Plus, maybe we can even find you a new wife

150
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,340
Let's get going

151
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,800
I can't do that

152
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:00,560
I've never even thought about remarrying

153
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:05,340
This is the worst day I've had since I was assigned Stein as a partner

154
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:07,660
This is not good, Blair, really

155
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:09,180
You're depressing the customer

156
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:13,980
It must be Scythe Meister Maka

157
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:18,420
Ow, my face!

158
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:21,420
Hmm, let's see, Scythe Meister Maka

159
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:23,700
Something's familiar about that name

160
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,400
If I could just put my finger on it

161
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,900
Ah, your mother was a meister

162
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:30,680
And you're spirit's little daughter, aren't you?

163
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,460
It was an absolute hell

164
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:35,220
The time I spent as his partner

165
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,880
Whose spirit?

166
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,040
That's what my father was called before he became a death scythe

167
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:43,080
But I want to know how you knew about that

168
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:45,380
I can still remember even now

169
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:47,240
He looked so peaceful in his sleep

170
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,180
That guy

171
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,860
He did

172
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:52,400
Experiments on my body

173
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,860
He used me as a lap rat while I was sleeping

174
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:58,500
And this went on for five years

175
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:01,040
Wow, for five years?

176
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:02,900
I can't believe you didn't notice anything

177
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,660
Oh, wow

178
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:06,460
You must have been really stupid back then

179
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:11,680
The only strange thing I noticed was that new scars would appear on my body every day

180
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:14,060
The parents' wife hadn't figured out what was going on

181
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,920
He might still be doing things to me

182
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,780
I can't stand to think about it even now

183
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:20,260
Ah, so

184
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:23,320
You are indeed spirit's darling little daughter

185
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:27,200
And the daughter of the woman who ended my greatest experiment

186
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,880
I wonder what kind of subject you'd make

187
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:34,180
But you were Stein's weapon partner for five whole years, weren't you?

188
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,200
Doesn't that mean your soul must have been compatible with his?

189
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:38,400
You don't understand

190
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:39,480
It doesn't matter

191
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:43,020
If he has any interest in a weapon, he can easily master it

192
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:45,560
He's much stronger and smarter than my wife

193
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,700
Sorry, ex-wife

194
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:49,080
The one who made me into a death scythe

195
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:52,780
Stein's mad, but he's a genius

196
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:55,180
It's just a tap

197
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,020
I can block it

198
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:56,620
Okay

199
00:09:56,620 --> 00:10:03,880
What?

200
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,080
What did he?

201
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,480
What the hell did he do to me?

202
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,320
I don't believe this

203
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:12,960
Sure, magic weapons have valuable physical attack properties

204
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:16,420
But primarily a Meister needs a weapon to channel his soul wavelength

205
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:18,000
But that man

206
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,200
He can attack with his soul directly

207
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,580
He doesn't need a weapon to access his power

208
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:28,400
Yep, the relationship between Meister and weapon is a lot like the relationship between a guitar and an amplifier

209
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:33,580
On its own, an electric guitar is only capable of emitting a small noise

210
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:40,500
But when you connect the guitar to an amplifier, you enhance the sound waves

211
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:43,020
And the result is much more powerful than before

212
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,800
Witch Hunter

213
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:49,340
The technique that Maka used in the battle against Cid is a perfect example of this

214
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:52,380
Even if she did fail with it in the end

215
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:58,620
But in Stein's case, he can use the guitar to make a huge noise without an amplifier

216
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:01,220
Oh, that's incredible

217
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:05,420
I can only imagine how strong he must be when he does use a weapon

218
00:11:05,420 --> 00:11:08,000
Let's see here

219
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,720
How should I begin my experiment?

220
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,260
What's wrong, Maka?

221
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,120
Chill out

222
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:16,100
Your soul waves are completely chaotic

223
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,820
Wait, Maka!

224
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:22,840
That was a dumb move!

225
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:33,020
Ah, you have lovely skin, simply lovely

226
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:37,440
Where do you think I should insert the knife first?

227
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:44,160
Let's see if I can turn your smooth skin into sandpaper

228
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:47,200
You're about to need a new pair of glasses, bastard

229
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,660
How could you have already forgotten that I'm here?

230
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:50,300
Easily

231
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:53,780
You're not the only one who can use soul waves to attack without a weapon

232
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:54,600
What?

233
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,120
Blackstar's big wave!

234
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:02,380
Amazing

235
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:04,060
He can do that?

236
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:08,620
He may appear to be a child, but Blackstar's soul wavelength is incredibly large

237
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:12,660
And for his age, he's a genius at using the direct soul attack against an opponent

238
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:18,260
Still, it won't do him much good in this fight

239
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:25,180
A surprise from the wild boy

240
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,020
What the hell is going on?

241
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,400
This is useless

242
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:31,460
You deflected my soul attack

243
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:35,260
Don't you remember how I checked your soul data when you first arrived here?

244
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:41,320
When I did that, I familiarized myself with your soul's wavelength, so now I can adjust mine so that they match

245
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:45,480
When the wavelengths are the same, they cancel each other out so your attack is powerless

246
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,460
You see, in the exact moment you attacked, we temporarily bonded

247
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:52,360
It's like the connection between a Meister and his weapon

248
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:54,680
A human can actually accomplish that

249
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:58,560
It's only possible if the human has a soul that is incredibly flexible

250
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,680
Stein does

251
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,840
That's one of the reasons that he is so difficult to defeat in a fight

252
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:06,240
That was a fun experiment, but now it's my turn

253
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:11,200
Blackstar!

254
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:14,640
Leave him alone!

255
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:42,000
This is too much

256
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,440
They need help, let's go

257
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,900
Okay, sure

258
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:45,880
Let's go!

259
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,340
Kid, you can't get involved

260
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:50,260
This is a test for them to complete on their own

261
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:51,920
Besides, you're a grim reaper

262
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:53,420
You're not a student here

263
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,780
All right

264
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:59,480
Then in that case, as of this moment, consider me enrolled

265
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:03,720
Dad, I would appreciate it if you would register me for classes

266
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,060
Liz, Patty?

267
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:05,960
Yes, kid!

268
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:08,080
Hey, all of you, come back here!

269
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,020
Oh, my, my

270
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:16,740
What did he do?

271
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:21,920
Tsubaki

